  "goodToKnow": "Die Tötung is killing, a neutral and legal term: die Tötung eines Menschen. German criminal law distinguishes Mord (murder), Totschlag (manslaughter), fahrlässige Tötung (negligent homicide, e.g. in a car accident) and Tötung auf Verlangen (killing on request, still a crime). In 2020 the Constitutional Court ruled that people have a right to assisted suicide, a separate and much-debated issue. Töten means to kill, and tot means dead."
